{"title":"2006 iTest Problems/Problem U1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_U1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the real number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> such that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/b/e6b65bac4a7c29faa1f80320d9f69fa1767bb77d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{x-9} + \\sqrt{x-6} = \\sqrt{x-1}.\\]\" width=\"219\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_U1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, square both sides to remove some radicals.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/4/0549ff507a789d492bdaf64ba4ba5ec686e54f2d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x-9 + 2\\sqrt{(x-9)(x-6)} + x-6 = x-1\\]\" width=\"330\" height=\"32\" />\nNext, combine terms, isolate the radical part, and square both sides.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/0/a40053acb89b3337d2ca4d68b665bac0c3f11ac3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} x-9 + 2\\sqrt{(x-9)(x-6)} + x-6 &amp;= x-1 \\\\ 2x - 15 + 2\\sqrt{(x-9)(x-6)} &amp;= x-1 \\\\ 2\\sqrt{(x-9)(x-6)} &amp;= -x+14 \\\\ 4(x^2 - 15x + 54) &amp;= x^2 - 28x + 196 \\end{align*}\" width=\"407\" height=\"137\" />\nSolve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> by combining terms into a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadratic\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Quadratic\">quadratic</a>.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/b/4dbc924400a0b812660f377bb36b06e3376dbda6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 4x^2 - 60x + 216 &amp;= x^2 - 28x + 196 \\\\ 3x^2 - 32x + 20 &amp;= 0 \\\\ (3x - 2)(x - 10) &amp;= 0 \\\\ x &amp;= \\tfrac23 , 10 \\end{align*}\" width=\"270\" height=\"101\" />\nBecause we squared both sides, we have to check for extraneous solutions. Of the two values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d98502509e862e72c463b55a42b95925ba25f1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"9\" height=\"21\" /> does not result in equality while <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> does. Thus, the real number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> that satisfies the equation is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/7/cd7ae6c302dec5c5be789f3d4d9be37d000d0772.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_U1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsectio